note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note bridge/shlib/gate.om: OMEGA-SHLIB, the gate of bridge/shlib (shared libraries written by Omega alone), in
note seeded Omega (Linux AArch64). Build from the repository root (OM-2 program mode; seed/ng/sha256.om supplies
note sh_dat, sh_all, sh_dig, sh_hexd):
note   { printf 'om2\n'; cat seed/ng/sha256.om bridge/shlib/gate.om; } | seed/out/omc > shlib-gate
note   seed/out/omc < bridge/shlib/shlib.om > shlib
note Run from the repository root: shlib-gate OMC SHLIB SCRATCH
note OMC      the compiler; its sha256 must equal the first word of seed/out/omc.sha256, or nothing runs (exit 69)
note SHLIB    the generator built from bridge/shlib/shlib.om
note SCRATCH  a new directory (created 0700); an existing one is refused (exit 2), and so is a path too long to hold
note          its files within Linux's 4096-byte PATH_MAX
note Checks, each an exact exit status: OMC compiles, in object mode (0), bridge/shlib/test.om, dep.om and imp.om,
note the test transport (rmfake.om then nvrmfake.om), libnvidia-ml.so.1's unit (gpu/nvidia/native/nvml's
note nvml.om, query.om, step.om and errstr.om, then bridge/shlib/nvml.om; errstr.om in its OM-2 view: the
note whole-word token "at", a reserved word of OM-2 and a parameter name there, becomes "at_" outside note lines)
note and libomega-ampere-qmd.so.1's unit (gpu/nvidia/om/encoder/amp_runtime.om and amp_qmd.om, then
note bridge/shlib/ampqmd.om); SHLIB writes each library (test, nvrmfake, nvml, dep, imp, ampqmd) and its probe
note (0); each probe, run by the system's
note dynamic loader from the scratch directory (so nvml finds the transport and imp finds dep through $ORIGIN),
note makes every call row of its table and gets the expected results with x19..x27, x29, d8..d15 and sp
note preserved (0);
note /usr/bin/readelf -W -S -d --dyn-syms reads each library through its section headers without a warning,
note shows the table's soname, every needed library of its table and lists every export of its table (0; readelf
note is a read-only verification
note oracle); the test library's wrappers hold four stack probes covering 3, 5, 1 and 2 pages, each fully formed
note with the wrapper's BL after it (0); each wrapper holds the 10 STP words that save x19..x30 and d8..d15, and
note the matching LDPs appear outside the wrappers (0); a second build of the test library from the same object holds the
note same bytes.
note Controls, each must be caught with its exact status (and, where named, its text in stderr):
note   row      a malformed call row (EXPECT 7x) appended to test.tsv: SHLIB refuses it (1, "malformed number")
note   float    the export row of omega_shlib_fl (an f64 export in test.om, not in test.tsv) appended to test.tsv:
note            SHLIB refuses it (1, "a float parameter or result")
note   export   omega_shlib_div's export row and its call rows removed from the library's table, the probe
note            (built from the full table) still needs it: the loader refuses the probe
note            (127, "undefined symbol: omega_shlib_div")
note   hash     every .hash bucket of the test library zeroed: no symbol resolves (127, "undefined symbol: ")
note   expect   the first call's EXPECT changed from 7 to 8: the probe reports call 0 (1)
note   stack    the shared return's ADD SP, SP, #192 turned into ADD SP, SP, #208, so every call returns with
note            sp 16 bytes high: the probe's stack check reports it (250)
note   extend   the wrappers' SXTW X0, W0 and SXTW X1, W1 turned into NOP: omc's int add finds the sum of -3 (zero
note            upper half) and 10 outside int and traps, so call 1 answers 999 for 7 (2)
note   uextend  every UXTW (UBFX X, X, #0, #32) turned into NOP: call 9 (a uint with a dirty upper half) fails (10)
note   nextend  every UXTB, UXTH, SXTB and SXTH turned into NOP: call 12 (a uchar with dirty upper bits) fails (13)
note   restore  the shared return's LDP X19, X20, [SP, #32] turned into [SP, #48]: x19 and x20 come back wrong (250)
note   runtime  one trap-entry load LDR X16, [X7, #16] in test.obj turned into [X7, #0], a runtime entry the
note            library does not provide: SHLIB refuses the object (1, "runtime entry")
note   need     the private function deep's frame in test.obj made 32 bytes smaller: the export's settled need
note            drops from 16400 to 16368 bytes, so its probe covers 4 pages, not 5: the stack probe check reports
note            it (1); the generator must accept the object
note   address  omega_shlib_seven's address in test.obj moved by 2 bytes: SHLIB refuses the object
note            (1, "a function address is outside the code")
note   frestore the shared return's LDP D8, D9, [SP, #128] turned into [SP, #144]: d8 and d9 come back wrong (250)
note   callrec  the last call record (edge's) dropped from test.obj: SHLIB refuses it (1, "a BL word has no call
note            record")
note   callto   the last call record's destination made omega_shlib_seven: SHLIB refuses it (1, "a call record's
note            destination is not its BL's target")
note   nosave   the first wrapper's STP X19, X20, [SP, #32] turned into NOP: the save check reports it (1)
note   readwarn .dynsym's section header sh_entsize made 25: readelf warns and still exits 0 (300)
note   readname omega_shlib_seven renamed omega_shlib_seveN in .dynstr: an export readelf does not list (301)
note   readsoname the soname's first byte in .dynstr made 'L': readelf shows another soname (302)
note   differ   a copy of the test library with its last byte changed: the same-bytes check finds a difference (1)
note   x7use    omega_shlib_seven's first word in test.obj made STR Q0, [X7]: SHLIB refuses the object
note            (1, "through the per-call context (x7)")
note   slot     the first entry slot's B in test.obj one word further: SHLIB refuses the object (1, "an export's
note            entry slot does not branch to its function")
note   map      imp.tsv's import row for omega_dep_sub without its swap (s0 s1): the dependency computes 3 - 5, so
note            call 7 fails (8)
note   noneed   imp.tsv without its needed row for libomshdep.so.1, the file still beside it: nothing loads it
note            (127, "undefined symbol: omega_dep_")
note   unlock   the import library's shared return without its UNLOCK call (its BLR X16 made NOP): the lock stays
note            held, pthread_mutex_trylock refuses call 1, which answers its TRAP value 999 (2)
note   improw   an import row for omega_nope appended to imp.tsv: SHLIB refuses it (1, "an import row names no
note            import")
note   frame    omega_imp_count's state ImpS dropped from its frame row (1, "a frame export's parameters do not
note            match its row")
note   lockexp  omega_imp_live exported without frame in the locked imp.tsv (1, "an export of a locked library is
note            not a frame export")
note   transport libnvidia-ml.so.1 and its probe in a directory without libomega-nvrm.so.1 (127,
note            "libomega-nvrm.so.1")
note   nvinit   the composed NVML source with nvmlInit_v2's body made nvmlShutdown's: nvmlInit_v2 (row 3)
note            answers NVML_ERROR_UNINITIALIZED for 0 (4)
note   readneed the import library's needed name in .dynstr made Libomshdep.so.1: readelf shows another needed
note            library (303)
note   stackarg the Ampere QMD library's frame word for the caller's stack arguments pointed at the frame instead
note            (ADD X16, SP, #288 made #96): the accepted build's QMD differs at buf+64 (30)
note   nvcopy   the composed NVML source copying text answers from the step state instead of the step buffer:
note            the name's first word differs (10)
note The extend, uextend, nextend and nosave controls change only the wrappers' words, found through .dynsym.
note Output: one line per check and control, then OMEGA-SHLIB PASS|FAIL checks=N controls=C caught=K.
note Exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 bad usage or setup, 69 compiler digest refused.
global g_pin uchar 64
